WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.867
The objects subsystem defines everything a scene can

00:00:06.967 --> 00:00:11.034
draw: meshes built from geometry and materials, five

00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:14.881
scientific primitives, and imported glTF assets.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.192
A mesh pairs one geometry with one

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:21.905
material, and gets its own transform.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:26.586
Geometry and materials are reference counted: createMesh takes

00:00:26.686 --> 00:00:29.816
over one reference and destroy releases it, so

00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:33.326
shared resources are retained once per extra mesh.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:38.196
Meshes form hierarchies with setParent and addChild, clones share

00:00:38.296 --> 00:00:43.041
the same resources, and castShadow and receiveShadow control shadows.

00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:49.707
Built-in primitives include boxes, spheres, cylinders, tori, prisms,

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:53.267
pyramids, planes, and flat shapes such as circles,

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:56.898
ellipses, rectangles, triangles, lines, and points.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.188
Cartesian and parametric curves and surfaces sample your

00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:06.032
functions; surfaces get triangles, normals, and texture coordinates.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:10.316
Custom geometry takes your own vertex and index arrays,

00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:14.589
and can borrow WebAssembly memory views for its attributes.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.891
Four material types share one interface: unlit for flat

00:01:20.991 --> 00:01:26.200
color, standard for glTF-style physically based shading, data for

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.202
colormapped values, and custom for your own WGSL.

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:34.668
A custom material declares its own resources in bind group

00:01:34.768 --> 00:01:38.448
one, because bind group zero belongs to the renderer.

00:01:38.866 --> 00:01:43.267
Textures upload asynchronously with mipmaps and sampler settings, and

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:46.660
render with fallback resources until they are ready.

00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:51.395
Colormaps come built in, viridis, plasma, magma, inferno, turbo,

00:01:51.495 --> 00:01:54.924
and grayscale, or from your own stops and palettes.

00:01:56.833 --> 00:01:59.560
PointCloud draws points colored by a scalar

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.386
through a colormap, or by per-point colors.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:07.288
GlyphField instances ellipsoids, arrows, or custom geometry,

00:02:07.388 --> 00:02:09.889
for example to show vector fields.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.106
NodeLink draws graphs, with separate scales

00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:15.405
and colormaps for nodes and edges.

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:21.453
SplatField draws Gaussian splats, optionally with spherical harmonics up to degree

00:02:21.553 --> 00:02:25.290
three, and is always transparent and sorted on the GPU.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.348
LatticeSpace draws regular 2D or 3D

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.253
cells, stored with x varying fastest.

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:35.977
All five borrow caller-supplied GPU buffers by default, and

00:02:36.077 --> 00:02:39.417
destroy them only with ownBuffers set to true.

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:46.780
gltf.load reads JSON or binary GLB files and their buffers,

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:53.926
gltf.import converts them into scene resources, and loadAndImport does both.

00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:58.650
Accessor decoding, sparse patching, and numeric conversion run

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.497
in Rust, and import covers material extensions, skins,

00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:05.988
animations, cameras, lights, and Gaussian splats.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.281
Each asset reports its support as supported, partial, deferred, or

00:03:11.381 --> 00:03:16.262
unsupported, and a failed import rolls back everything it created.

00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:21.986
Animation clips sample translation, rotation, and scale

00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:24.907
channels in Rust, while morph weights and

00:03:25.007 --> 00:03:28.114
animation pointers are sampled in TypeScript.

00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:32.130
Players advance clips with looping and speed, and skins

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.558
drive four- or eight-influence skinning on the GPU.

00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:38.736
Morph targets blend positions, normals, and

00:03:38.836 --> 00:03:41.072
colors, and update the mesh bounds.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.516
To recap: reference-counted meshes, built-in and custom geometry, four

00:03:48.616 --> 00:03:53.972
material types, five scientific primitives, and glTF with animation.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.630
The full reference is in the Objects section of the documentation.
